# The night-lights texture, copied out of node_modules by
# scripts/copy-textures.mjs. Kept out of git so a 700 KB binary does not live in
# history; it arrives with npm install and is copied before dev and build. It
# was five files until the globe renderer was deleted (D104) -- the other four
# lit a three.js sphere that no longer exists.
frontend/public/textures/

# Session handoff notes. Local working state that tracks in-progress status and
# open bugs, not a committed artifact — it goes stale the moment it is shared.
HANDOFF.md

# ICAO airline designators, reduced out of node_modules by
# scripts/build-airlines.mjs. Generated, for the same reason.
frontend/public/data/

# Orbital elements cached between runs, so a restart during an upstream
# outage still has something to propagate. Derived data with a network source.
#
# Two paths because the cache is relative to the working directory, and the
# backend has two supported ones: `backend/` when uvicorn is run from there,
# and the repository root when it is run with `--app-dir backend`, which is
# what `.claude/launch.json` does. Ignoring only the first would have committed
# a 450 KB element blob the first time anyone used the launch config.
backend/.cache/
/.cache/

# scroll-craft, vendored from github.com/nateherkai/scroll-craft (MIT).
#
# An agent skill for building scroll-driven landing pages: 441 KB of someone
# else's design methodology, kept on this machine so the tooling can load it
# and deliberately not committed. It is not part of Orbital, it would be the
# largest thing in a repository submitted as our own work, and anyone who wants
# it can install it from upstream in one command.
#
# `.claude/launch.json` stays tracked - only the skills directory is ignored.
.claude/skills/

# Its build workspace, which it creates beside the repository root. Generated
# output with a third-party generator, and some of it is video.
/scrollcraft/
